---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import "../../styles/global.css";
---

<Layout
	title="Single Right Triangle Problems | Applications of Trigonometry | Class 10 | The Concepts Adda"
	description="Solve single right-angled triangle heights and distances problems (towers, broken trees, kite strings) step by step for Class 10 NCERT."
>
	<main class="lesson-page">
		<div class="lesson-container">
			<a href="/applications-of-trigonometry" class="back-link">
				<span class="back-arrow">←</span>
				<span>Back to Applications of Trigonometry</span>
			</a>

			<!-- LESSON HEADER -->
			<section class="lesson-header">
				<div class="lesson-number">02</div>
				<div class="lesson-header-copy">
					<div class="lesson-label">LESSON 02 · CLASS 10 MATHEMATICS (NCERT)</div>
					<h1>Single Right <span>Triangle Problems</span></h1>
					<p>
						Solve heights and distances problems involving a single right-angled triangle step by step with NCERT examples.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- CONTENT LAYOUT -->
			<section class="content-layout">
				<article class="lesson-content">

					<!-- 01 · GENERAL APPROACH -->
					<div class="topic-label">01 · SOLVING APPROACH</div>
					<h2>3 Steps to Solve Single Triangle Questions</h2>

					<div class="summary-list">
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>Step 1</span>
							<p>Draw the ground level, height (vertical line), and line of sight to form △ABC with ∠B = 90°.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>Step 2</span>
							<p>Identify the given side and the side to find (Opposite, Adjacent, or Hypotenuse).</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>Step 3</span>
							<p>Apply <strong>tan θ</strong>, <strong>sin θ</strong>, or <strong>cos θ</strong> and solve for the unknown side.</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- 02 · SOLVED NCERT EXAMPLES -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">02 · SOLVED NCERT EXAMPLES</div>
					<h2>Step-by-Step Problem Solving</h2>

					<!-- Example 1 -->
					<div class="example-card">
						<div class="example-header">
							<span class="example-badge">EXAMPLE 1 · TOWER HEIGHT</span>
							<h3>A tower stands vertically on ground. From a point 15 m away from foot, angle of elevation of top is 60°. Find height.</h3>
						</div>
						<div class="example-solution">
							<!-- SVG Diagram -->
							<div style="margin:15px 0; text-align:center;">
								<svg width="340" height="200" viewBox="0 0 340 200" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="background:#f8fafc; border-radius:18px; border:1px solid #cbd5e1; box-shadow:0 6px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.03);">
									<!-- Ground Line -->
									<line x1="30" y1="160" x2="310" y2="160" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2"/>
									<!-- Tower (Vertical) -->
									<line x1="260" y1="40" x2="260" y2="160" stroke="#0f172a" stroke-width="3.5"/>
									<!-- Line of Sight -->
									<line x1="50" y1="160" x2="260" y2="40" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="3"/>

									<!-- Right Angle Symbol -->
									<path d="M 248,160 L 248,148 L 260,148" stroke="#0f172a" stroke-width="1.5" fill="none"/>

									<!-- Angle Arc -->
									<path d="M 90 160 A 40 40 0 0 0 85 140" stroke="#dc2626" stroke-width="2.5" fill="none"/>
									<text x="96" y="152" fill="#dc2626" font-size="13" font-weight="900">60°</text>

									<!-- Points -->
									<circle cx="50" cy="160" r="4.5" fill="#2563eb"/>
									<circle cx="260" cy="160" r="4.5" fill="#0f172a"/>
									<circle cx="260" cy="40" r="4.5" fill="#0f172a"/>

									<!-- Labels -->
									<text x="35" y="180" fill="#0f172a" font-size="14" font-weight="900">A (Observer)</text>
									<text x="265" y="180" fill="#0f172a" font-size="14" font-weight="900">B (Foot)</text>
									<text x="265" y="32" fill="#0f172a" font-size="14" font-weight="900">C (Top)</text>
									<text x="140" y="180" fill="#2563eb" font-size="13" font-weight="800">Ground = 15 m</text>
									<text x="272" y="105" fill="#0f172a" font-size="13" font-weight="800">h = ?</text>
								</svg>
							</div>

							<p>Let height of tower = <em>h</em>, distance from foot = 15 m, angle θ = 60°.</p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								tan 60° = Opposite / Adjacent = h / 15<br/>
								√3 = h / 15 ⟹ <strong>h = 15√3 metres</strong>
							</div>
							<p style="margin-top:10px;">Height of tower is <strong>15√3 m</strong> (≈ 25.98 m).</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- Example 2 -->
					<div class="example-card">
						<div class="example-header">
							<span class="example-badge">EXAMPLE 2 · BROKEN TREE PROBLEM</span>
							<h3>A tree breaks due to storm and broken top touches ground making an angle of 30°. Distance from foot to top on ground is 8 m. Find total height of tree.</h3>
						</div>
						<div class="example-solution">
							<!-- SVG Diagram -->
							<div style="margin:15px 0; text-align:center;">
								<svg width="340" height="210" viewBox="0 0 340 210" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="background:#f8fafc; border-radius:18px; border:1px solid #cbd5e1; box-shadow:0 6px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.03);">
									<!-- Ground Line -->
									<line x1="30" y1="170" x2="310" y2="170" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2"/>
									<!-- Unbroken Trunk h1 -->
									<line x1="240" y1="100" x2="240" y2="170" stroke="#15803d" stroke-width="4"/>
									<!-- Original Tree Top (Dashed) -->
									<line x1="240" y1="30" x2="240" y2="100" stroke="#16a34a" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-dasharray="4,4"/>
									<!-- Broken Slanting Part h2 -->
									<line x1="60" y1="170" x2="240" y2="100" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="3.5"/>

									<!-- Right Angle Symbol -->
									<path d="M 228,170 L 228,158 L 240,158" stroke="#0f172a" stroke-width="1.5" fill="none"/>

									<!-- Angle Arc -->
									<path d="M 100 170 A 40 40 0 0 0 95 156" stroke="#dc2626" stroke-width="2.5" fill="none"/>
									<text x="105" y="165" fill="#dc2626" font-size="13" font-weight="900">30°</text>

									<!-- Points -->
									<circle cx="60" cy="170" r="4.5" fill="#2563eb"/>
									<circle cx="240" cy="170" r="4.5" fill="#0f172a"/>
									<circle cx="240" cy="100" r="4.5" fill="#15803d"/>

									<!-- Labels -->
									<text x="35" y="190" fill="#0f172a" font-size="14" font-weight="900">A (Top on ground)</text>
									<text x="248" y="190" fill="#0f172a" font-size="14" font-weight="900">B (Foot)</text>
									<text x="248" y="105" fill="#15803d" font-size="14" font-weight="900">C (Broken Point)</text>
									<text x="248" y="28" fill="#16a34a" font-size="13" font-weight="700">Original Top</text>
									<text x="130" y="190" fill="#2563eb" font-size="13" font-weight="800">8 m</text>
									<text x="252" y="140" fill="#15803d" font-size="13" font-weight="800">h₁</text>
									<text x="140" y="125" fill="#2563eb" font-size="13" font-weight="800" transform="rotate(-21, 140, 125)">h₂ (Broken Part)</text>
								</svg>
							</div>

							<p>Let unbroken part = <em>h₁</em>, broken slanting part = <em>h₂</em>. Distance = 8 m, θ = 30°.</p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								tan 30° = h₁ / 8 ⟹ 1/√3 = h₁ / 8 ⟹ <strong>h₁ = 8 / √3</strong><br/>
								cos 30° = 8 / h₂ ⟹ √3/2 = 8 / h₂ ⟹ <strong>h₂ = 16 / √3</strong>
							</div>
							<p style="margin-top:12px;">Total Height = h₁ + h₂ = 8/√3 + 16/√3 = 24/√3 = <strong>8√3 metres</strong>.</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- 03 · QUICK SUMMARY -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">03 · QUICK SUMMARY</div>
					<h2>Key Takeaways</h2>

					<div class="summary-list">
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>01</span>
							<p>When height and distance are involved, use <strong>tan θ = Height / Distance</strong>.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>02</span>
							<p>When slant length / string length is involved, use <strong>sin θ = Height / Slant Length</strong>.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>03</span>
							<p>Always rationalise denominators (e.g. 24/√3 = 8√3).</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- LESSON NAVIGATION -->
					<div class="lesson-navigation">
						<a href="/applications-of-trigonometry/line-of-sight-elevation-depression" class="previous-lesson">
							<span>←</span>
							<div>
								<small>PREVIOUS LESSON</small>
								<strong>Line of Sight & Angles</strong>
							</div>
						</a>

						<a href="/applications-of-trigonometry/double-triangle-problems" class="next-lesson">
							<div>
								<small>NEXT LESSON</small>
								<strong>Double Triangle Problems</strong>
							</div>
							<span>→</span>
						</a>
					</div>
				</article>

				<!-- SIDEBAR -->
				<aside class="lesson-sidebar">
					<div class="sidebar-card">
						<div class="sidebar-title">APPLICATIONS OF TRIGONOMETRY</div>
						<div class="progress-text">Lesson 02 of 04</div>
						<div class="progress-bar">
							<div style="width: 50%;"></div>
						</div>

						<div class="sidebar-lessons">
							<a href="/applications-of-trigonometry/line-of-sight-elevation-depression" class="sidebar-lesson">
								<span>01</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Line of Sight & Angles</strong>
									<small>Elevation & depression rules</small>
								</div>
							</a>

							<a href="/applications-of-trigonometry/single-triangle-problems" class="sidebar-lesson active">
								<span>02</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Single Triangle Problems</strong>
									<small>Height & distance calculations</small>
								</div>
							</a>

							<a href="/applications-of-trigonometry/double-triangle-problems" class="sidebar-lesson">
								<span>03</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Double Triangle Problems</strong>
									<small>2-triangle NCERT word problems</small>
								</div>
							</a>

							<a href="/applications-of-trigonometry/pyqs" class="sidebar-lesson">
								<span>04</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Previous Year PYQs</strong>
									<small>CBSE 2020-2024 practice set</small>
								</div>
							</a>
						</div>
					</div>
				</aside>
			</section>
		</div>
	</main>

